wip/py-taichi: Import taichi-1.7.4

Taichi Lang is a Python-embedded language for parallel numerical
computation.  Only the Metal backend is built (TI_WITH_LLVM=OFF): the
LLVM-based CPU/CUDA backends need LLVM 15, which pkgsrc lacks.  Kernels
are compiled to SPIR-V, translated to MSL with SPIRV-Cross and compiled
at run time by Metal; a SAXPY test runs at about 265 GB/s on the M5
Pro.  The GGUI (Vulkan) window system is not built; ti.GUI works.

Pinned git submodules are fetched as GITHUB_SUBMODULES; Eigen comes
from math/eigen3.  The bundled SPIRV-Tools/SPIRV-Cross are not
installed, -Werror is dropped, and the upstream build.py is renamed so
it does not shadow the PEP 517 "build" module.
